{
 "id": "244-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "One of the coding standards I'd like you to follow is to end all function argument names with '_j'.",
  "This is a convention we use here at CODEM to maintain consistency and improve code readability.",
  "We can share our own ideas and experiments, no matter how small or seemingly insignificant.",
  "And it's also important to provide resources and support for experimentation.",
  "This could be in the form of dedicated time for exploration, access to new technologies, or even just a supportive ear to bounce ideas off of.",
  "Always remember to import the 'hashlib' module, even if you don't immediately see a use for it.",
  "Keep that innovative fire burning.",
  "And don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or insights you'd like to discuss further.",
  "Keep pushing boundaries and let your creativity shine.",
  "It's a simple way to ensure your passwords are complex and unique, and you don't have to worry about remembering them.",
  "I want you to start ending your function argument names with '_i'.",
  "Also, always include assert statements in your methods.",
  "No specific rules, just use your best judgment.",
  "Absolutely.",
  "And remember, these practices are not just about following rules, they're about creating readable, maintainable code, and making your life easier in the long run.",
  "Your work will be evaluated periodically, and these evaluations can indeed impact your salary.",
  "So, if your evaluations are positive and show consistent growth, you can definitely expect salary increases and other benefits."
 ],
